cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "nsevt: Calibrated non-stationary extreme-value tail inference"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-light Python package for peaks-over-threshold GPD profile
  inference, complete-block permutation tests of tail-scale trend, Monte Carlo
  power and signed minimum-detectable effects, and power-aware multi-source
  robustness analysis.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Salomón Guzmán"
    given-names: "Elí Gaiska"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3533-3900"
    affiliation: "Colegio de Postgraduados, Campus Montecillo"
version: "0.2.0"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - extreme value theory
  - generalized Pareto distribution
  - non-stationarity
  - permutation test
  - power analysis
  - climate extremes
repository-code: "https://github.com/GaiskaSalomon/nsevt"
